## destroy (body-3)

Unregisters descriptor listener, calls every instantiated command destroy without awaiting returned promises, clears Set, awaits descriptor destruction if needed, and closes client only when shouldCloseClient is true.

- reads: Set; descriptor isDestroyed; shouldCloseClient; client
- writes: Listener removed; commands and descriptor/client released
- branches: Skips missing destroy methods/already-destroyed descriptor/client-close-disabled branch.
- result: Promise resolving after awaited descriptor/client cleanup.
- errors: An inner throw aborts later cleanup; awaited rejections propagate.
- async: Inner destroys are invoked synchronously; descriptor and close are awaited.
- ownership: Releases command Set and fronts via descriptor; avoids recursing into already destroyed descriptor.

